.TH SYLVE-CONFIG 5 "2026-10-28" "sylve-cli @VERSION@" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
sylve-config \- configuration file format for sylve(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/sylve/config.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration file is YAML. It stores named contexts and the active
context. Each context contains the server URL and the session token.
.PP
The file is written with mode 0600. Keep it private.
.SH FORMAT
.nf
current_context: prod

contexts:
  prod:
    server: https://sylve.example.test
    username: admin
    auth_type: sylve
    node_id: node-uuid
    hostname: node1.example.test
    token: eyJ...
    expires_at: "2026-11-01T12:00:00Z"
    verify_ssl: true
    ca_cert: null
    default_node: node1.example.test
.fi
.PP
See also the Markdown version at
.I docs/config-format.md .
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B current_context
Name of the context used when
.B \-\-context
is not supplied.
.TP
.B contexts
Mapping of context names to context objects.
.TP
.B server
Base URL of the Sylve API. The
.I /api
suffix is optional.
.TP
.B username
Login name recorded for the context.
.TP
.B auth_type
.I sylve
or
.IR pam .
.TP
.B token
Bearer token. Prefer
.B sylve login
over editing this field manually.
.TP
.B expires_at
Optional ISO-8601 token expiry. If omitted, the expiry is read from the JWT.
.TP
.B verify_ssl
Set to false only for self-signed test systems.
.TP
.B ca_cert
Optional path to a CA certificate.
.TP
.B default_node
Optional default target node.
.SH ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES
.TP
.B SYLVE_SERVER
Overrides the context server.
.TP
.B SYLVE_TOKEN
Overrides the context token.
.TP
.B SYLVE_NODE
Overrides the default node.
.TP
.B SYLVE_INSECURE
Set to 1, true, or yes to disable TLS verification.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sylve login https://sylve.example.test -u admin
sylve config get-contexts
sylve config use-context prod
sylve --context prod node list
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sylve (1),
.br
.BR sylve-config-format (7)
.br
.I docs/config-format.md \-
Markdown version of this page.
.SH NOTES
Manpage source:
.I docs/man/src/sylve-config.5.in
.br
Update the source when the CLI changes, then regenerate with:
.B make man
